cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  A Multi-Agent, Human-in-the-Loop Framework for Correcting
  Natural-Language-to-SQL Errors at Run Time
message: >-
  If you use this software or build on it, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yijing
    family-names: Wang
    affiliation: >-
      College of Computing and Data Science, Nanyang Technological
      University
abstract: >-
  An interactive error-correction framework for natural-language-to-SQL.
  Given the residual errors of a strong NL2SQL baseline, with no gold
  query available at run time, agents organised by SQL decision point
  enumerate candidate queries; the candidates are executed and clustered
  by result; and a triage policy decides, for each error, whether to
  repair it automatically on an objective signal, consult the user (who
  chooses between result tables, never SQL), or abstain. The design
  combines decision-point structural agents with error-type semantic
  agents, and confines the LLM to proposing candidates and phrasing
  questions.
keywords:
  - text-to-SQL
  - NL2SQL
  - human-in-the-loop
  - multi-agent systems
  - large language models
  - BIRD benchmark
  - error correction
